{"name":"Glow Worm","hex":"#bed565","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glow-worm","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of glowworm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow-worm"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glowworm","blocks":[{"text":"Glowworm is any member of various groups of insect larvae and adult larviform females that glow through bioluminescence. They include the European common glow-worm and other members of the Lampyridae, but bioluminescence also occurs in the families Elateridae, Phengodidae and Rhagophthalmidae among beetles; as well as members of the genera Arachnocampa, Keroplatus and Orfelia among keroplatid fungus gnats."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glowworm","wikidata":"Q3248829"},{"title":"Worm","blocks":[{"text":"Worms are many different distantly related bilateral animals that typically have a long cylindrical tube-like body, no limbs, and usually no eyes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Regenwurm1.jpg/330px-Regenwurm1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Worm","wikidata":"Q47253"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Glowworm_%284213020277%29.jpg/250px-Glowworm_%284213020277%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Glowworm_%284213020277%29.jpg/500px-Glowworm_%284213020277%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Glowworm_%284213020277%29.jpg/250px-Glowworm_%284213020277%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlowworm_(4213020277).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Firefly_Nevit_02670_cr.jpg/250px